# Egress allowlist for net-interpose (docs/boxing.md, "Network interpose").
# Empty means default-deny: the boxed client reaches nothing off-box.
#
# One entry per line, optionally with :PORT:
#   name            exact DNS name
#   *.suffix        any name under suffix (and suffix itself)
#   a.b.c.d[/n]     IPv4 address or CIDR
#
# Leave this empty in the repo. For the login spike (manual, disposable account),
# mount a filled-in copy over /etc/kakao/net-allowlist. Start from the names
# verify-net.sh lists as "client-denied".
